---
// The role, in one line (copy book B.17 + the reframes). By this point the
// page has already said what holding space means in plain words — the lyric
// is the distillation, and the by-line keeps it readable for someone meeting
// the term today. Both lines are slots; the defaults are the professional
// door's. The heal-the-healer door passes Jacob's own "You are the healer,
// and you are the healed" (quote bank #56 — safe to attribute).
---

<section class="we-lyric">
  <div class="we-lyric-inner">
    <img class="we-lyric-mark" src="/brand/symbol-orange.png" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
    <p class="we-lyric-text">
      <slot name="text">Not a healer — a space holder. We make room. The rest happens.</slot>
    </p>
    <div class="we-lyric-by">
      <slot name="by">— Your role in this work, in one line</slot>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
